  "evidence_boundary": "One new full18 R111 model, not an arm comparison. Fixed source-lineage families; P(method)=P(family)*P(method|family), normalized over the complete legal pool. Each family has two private full-node EncoderLayer self-attention/FFN layers before pooling, not single-query readout after pooling. Root reads only shared h/context and group-mean method tokens (plus family identity); private features do not feed back into root/shared joint/context. One unweighted NLL on normalized log probabilities; no second softmax, donor, teacher or auxiliary objective. Wrong-family private classification gradients are zero, not necessarily AdamW weight-decay/momentum updates. Shared features are not gradient-isolated. Singleton conditional probability is one; its private features may be skipped. All legal joint probabilities compete at inference; no hard family routing or winner-driven forward. Two4090 DDP, one group, global1024/local512; 57600 updates, warmup4320, AdamW1e-4 to1e-6, seed2. Original R84 frozen NEW90k data/cache and legal pools, TRAIN81000/VAL4500/TEST4500 per task. TRAIN-only SBS and per-instance legal-pool Oracle; ALL task-equal, mixed raw cost descriptive only. Native FP64 ind is the main winner, FP32 argmin only compatibility. One strict-first minimum full18 VAL macro_vs_sbs checkpoint for TRAIN/VAL/TEST/LIB, no reselection. Historical R84A/R94B and any R110 summaries are not newly trained, parameter- or FLOP-matched controls. NSS is saved R79 historical weights on exact NEW4500 TEST/native LIB, not new90k retraining. TEST has participated in development. Mechanism approval is not evidence of performance: single-arm historical comparisons remain provisional, with no causal or performance-gain claim. Optional timing is included only from an existing same-lock receipt; no benchmark is launched, and GPU-resident timing is not end-to-end dataset/solver latency.",
